📦 Supply Chain Costing System
Excel Automation + Python ETL + MySQL Database

This project delivers a complete end-to-end costing solution combining Excel automation, Python ETL, and a fully normalised MySQL database.
It replaces fragmented costing spreadsheets with a centralised, automated, and auditable system used to calculate deal costs, gross profit, and cash-flow projections.

🚀 Overview

The system integrates multiple data sources to produce accurate and consistent costing outputs:

Excel Costing Tool (Power Query + VBA automation)

SAP SQL Queries for real-time master data

Python ETL Pipeline (Monday.com → Excel → MySQL)

MySQL Supply Chain Costing Database for reporting & analysis

It supports finance, sales, and operations by creating a single source of truth for stock, transport, ad-hoc cost, sales, cash flow, and GP calculations.

🧩 Key Components
1️⃣ Excel Costing Workbook

Automated costing template built with Power Query

41 VBA modules for quoting, PDF export, Outlook emails, sheet protection, and logging

Captures full deal structure (stock, transport, ad-hoc, finance, GP)

Generates single- and multi-product quotes in minutes

2️⃣ Python ETL Pipeline

Fetches deal information from Monday.com via GraphQL API

Merges with Excel-based cost sheets

Cleans, transforms, and validates all values

Loads into MySQL using upsert logic

Full logging for traceability

3️⃣ MySQL Costing Database

Fully normalised 3NF schema

Tables for deals, stock cost, transport cost, ad-hoc cost, sales lines, cash flows

Lookup tables for products, clients, sales reps, uom, deal status, and transporters

Supports financial modelling and Power BI reporting

🛠️ Tech Stack

Excel: Power Query (M), VBA, Pivot Tables

Python: Pandas, Requests, openpyxl, mysql-connector

Database: MySQL 8.0

APIs: Monday.com GraphQL

Reporting: Power BI (GP analysis, sales conversion, forecasting)

📊 What the System Delivers

Standardised costing across all deals

Automated quote generation (PDF + email)

Centralised and auditable deal history

Integrated view of cost, sales, and cash flow

Power BI dashboards for profitability insights

🧠 Impact

Reduced quote turnaround time from hours to minutes

Eliminated version-control issues across costing files

Improved financial accuracy and forecasting

Enabled advanced reporting from a clean, structured database
